# Slack Modal Trigger Safety

Slack `trigger_id` values are time-sensitive. In handlers that open modals with
`client.views_open(...)`, do not perform external API calls, Slack API calls,
DB/cache queries, Redis calls, file downloads, or other awaited I/O before the
modal opens.

Open or respond immediately, then do slow work after:

- Open a lightweight/loading modal first, then call `views_update(...)`.
- Or respond/post a message immediately and continue work later.
- Keep deleted/inaccessible Slack file checks in submit/download paths, not
  modal-open triggers.

Avoid before `views_open(...)`:

- `client.files_info(...)`
- `get_accessible_slack_files(...)`
- `download_file(...)`
- Ray, Verify, or LanguageCloud API calls
- Redis/database/settings lookups unless already cached in context

When reviewing modal-trigger changes, audit every `await` between `ack()` and
`views_open(...)`.
